"/us/en/sage/urine-management/stop-urinary-incontinence-device-leaks": {"template":"base","metadata":{"title":"Start using PrimaFit – a urine management solution designed to stop leaks and limit CAUTIs","pageTitle":"Start using PrimaFit – a urine management solution designed to stop leaks and limit CAUTIs","description":"PrimaFit is designed to help improve operational efficiency and reduce costs. Traditional indwelling catheters can cause discomfort, skin injury and infection. ","image":"/content/dam/stryker/sage/urine-management/primafit-competitor/images/um-prima-campaign-mobile.jpg","imageAlt":"Nurse holding PrimaFit External Urine Management Device for the Female Anatomy","tags":["stryker:product/sage/Sage-PrimaFit","stryker:product/sage/Sage_PrimoFit","stryker:business-unit/SAGE"],"originallyPublished":"2024-09-25T20:57:38.000Z","lastPublished":"2026-08-20T19:51:30.000Z","contentID":"SAGE-UM-SYK-1231833_REV-1_en_us"},"anchors":[{"id":"proven","title":"Proven","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"par"},{"id":"benefits","title":"Benefits","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"par"},{"id":"contact","title":"Contact","hidden":true,"type":"section-title","area":"par"}],"disclaimer":"<p><b>References:</b></p>\r\n<p><b>1. </b>Loveday HP, Wilson JA, Pratt RJ, et al (2014) epic 3: national evidence-based guidelines for preventing healthcare associated infections in NHS hospitals in England. J Hosp Infect 86(Suppl 1): S1–S70.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><b>2.</b> Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, Catheter-associated Urinary Tract Infections (CAUTIs). Available at https://www.cdc.gov/hai/ca_uti/uti.html. Accessed August 24, 2017.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><b>3.</b> Beeson T, Davis C, Vollman K, Chasing Zero Catheter Associated Urinary Tract Infections (CAUTIs) through Implementing a Novel Female External Urine Collection Device in a Tertiary Academic Surgical Intensive Care Unit (SICU) Presented at APIC 2018.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><b>4</b>.&nbsp;Sage PrimaFit Instructions for use (IFU) 678907, 2023 and Sage PrimoFit+ Instructions for use (IFU) 843801, 2024.</p>\r\n<p><b>5.</b> Data on file, Sage Products LLC, Results pulled from 30 facilities total cost of ownership survey data collection. Retrieved August 8, 2022.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><b>6</b>.&nbsp;Data on file, Sage Products LLC. CMR 29283 CustomerOne Report</p>\r\n<p><b>7.</b>&nbsp;Sage Products, LLC. Data on file, 05 2026.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><b>8.</b> Data on file, Sage Products LLC, Product Evaluation C1 Summary 230328.&nbsp;</p>","forms":[{"formId":"1259","afterSubmitAction":"redirectToPage","message":null,"useProduction":true}],"tabs":[["Product information","Ordering info","Product support"]],"cardLists":[{"component":"customizable","title":null,"items":[{"path":"/us/en/sage/news/2024/shea-cauti-prevention-practice-updates","resolved":true,"title":"Strategies to prevent Catheter-Associated Urinary Tract Infections (CAUTIs)","description":"The Compendium offers updated guidance for hospitals to help reduce the risk of catheter-associated urinary tract infections (CAUTIs).","image":"/content/dam/stryker/sage/news/2024/catheter-stock-image_1440.jpg","alt":"Syringes and other catheter insertion devices"},{"path":"/us/en/sage/news/2023/external-urine-collection-device-JWOCN-study","resolved":true,"title":"Sage PrimaFit External Urine Management System for the Female Anatomy helped reduce CAUTI rate 63% ","description":"Catheter-related infections decreased from before the introduction to EUDFA and after. This is not a cause-and-effect relationship, but the trend is promising.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/sage/urine-management/images/primafit-video-thumbnail.png","alt":"PrimaFit External Urine Management for the Female Anatomy photo of application"},{"path":"/us/en/sage/news/2024/reduce-cauti-risk","resolved":true,"title":"Reduce the risk of catheter-associated urinary tract infection (CAUTI) in hospitals  ","description":"Catheter-associated urinary tract infections (CAUTIs) are among the most common types of healthcare-associated infections, and reducing them is beneficial to hospitals, caregivers and patients.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/sage/news/2024/CAUTI Illustration.jpg","alt":"CAUTI Illustration"},{"path":"/us/en/sage/news/2023/nyc-medical-center-implementation-of-external-female-catheter-av","resolved":true,"title":"NYC Medical Center Implementation of External Female Catheter avoids  $16M in costs over 2 years ","description":"In 2018, the implementation of the external female urine management device was introduced as a standard of nursing care as an alternative to an indwelling urinary catheter. Data captured in 2019 and 2020 showed utilization of the external female device to be 36% and 46%, respectively.","image":"/content/dam/stryker/sage/news/2023/23-SGC-712791-June_Newsroom3.jpg","alt":"23-SGC-712791-June_Newsroom3"}]}],"missingAlt":[]},
